   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization of the\ncounty of Onondaga to impose an additional rate of sales and compensating use\ntaxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S5512",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5512-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5512\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\nof the county of Onondaga to impose an additional rate of sales and\ncompensating use taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the County of Onondaga to impose a one percent sales tax\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes Onondaga County to impose a one percent sales tax\nthrough November 30, 2025.\n\nSections 2 and 3 outline how the revenue is to be allocated.\n\nSection 4 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is being introduced at the request of the County of Onondaga,\nin order to extend the current sales tax, which is set to expire Novem-\nber 30, 2025.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect immediately.\n",
